# gear.rec: the armour, every kind a record here and nowhere else (rogue/kinds.go reads it);
# a new record is a new armour. mktiles.py cuts the pictures onto tiles16.png and fills in
# the icons, the remapper (remap_gear.sh) re-maps them; every other field is yours.
# icon: cell of tiles16.png; -1: unassigned. picture: the source picture.
#
#   ac        armour class (lower is better)       prob: the chance of a found armour being this kind, of 100
#   worth     what the fighters guild pays          skin: the hobbit armour layer set (assets/hobbit/armor/<skin>_1 and _2)
#   helmet, chest, leggings, boots: the meshes.rec pieces the inventory hero wears (the Epic Knights models)

%rec: Tileset
id: tiles16
name: VoxelRogue 16px tiles
file: tiles16.png
tile_w: 16
tile_h: 16
off_x: 0
off_y: 0
gap_x: 0
gap_y: 0
meshes: meshes.rec

%rec: gear
%doc: Armour

id: leather armor
name: leather armor
picture: ../hobbit/bodyDunlending.png
icon: 0
ac: 8
prob: 20
worth: 5
skin: dunlending
chest: gambeson_chestplate
leggings: pantyhose
boots: gambeson_boots

